ough if any of those are unique identifiers...", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/631476546/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/631527589", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1103#issuecomment-631527589", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1103", "id": 631527589, "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzMTUyNzU4OQ==", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-05-20T14:57:08Z", "updated_at": "2020-05-20T14:57:08Z", "body": "Yes, I was looking at that today. The `msg_id`s can be duplicate but the `cookie` is unique, however, the unregistering won't happen very often.\r\n\r\nAnecdotally, I've heard that just looping through a relatively short `std::vector` can be quicker in practice than having to do lookups in a map, so I would try to profile it before changing.", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/631527589/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/631571984", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1103#issuecomment-631571984", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1103", "id": 631571984, "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzMTU3MTk4NA==", "user": {"login": "roangel", "id": 21340299, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzQwMjk5", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21340299?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel", "html_url": "https://github.com/roangel", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/roangel/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-05-20T16:07:10Z", "updated_at": "2020-05-20T16:07:10Z", "body": "\r\n\r\n> Anecdotally, I've heard that just looping through a relatively short `std::vector` can be quicker in practice than having to do lookups in a map, so I would try to profile it before changing.\r\n\r\nYes, I have als